Changelog:
==========

**v5.1 Beta 3** (public beta / release candidate for final validation)
New:
- central Web UI with PAM login, responsive configuration, filter previews, External management, Jobs, Logs, and running-job visibility
- session-independent systemd-run jobs for checks and updates, including shared history, locking, reload persistence, and remote-node dispatch
- QEMU Guest Agent and SSH transport support for VM checks and updates, including remote VM lifecycle handling
- configurable Proxmox backup storage selection through `BACKUP_STORAGE`; an empty value keeps automatic storage selection
- HTTPS-first Web UI operation on port 8765 with automatic Proxmox certificate use when available and HTTP fallback in auto mode
- External Linux APT and DNF support with dedicated SSH identity, non-root checks, restricted helper/sudo, local settings, and global Check/Update integration
- target-local External settings with independent `ONLY_UPDATE_CHECK`, `EXCLUDE_UPDATE_CHECK`, `ONLY`, and `EXCLUDE` filters
- deterministic golden-output regression tests and a reusable multi-hour Hardcore-Test specification, journal, and controlled stop workflow

Improved:
- cluster-wide installation and remote execution across Proxmox nodes, including offline/recovery handling and friendly target names
- separate Check/Update filters and read-only previews with `ONLY` precedence over `EXCLUDE`
- Global Update selection now includes managed External targets while applying central filters before any remote contact
- checks and updates now preserve running, stopped, and paused VM/LXC lifecycle state, including restore after failures
- concurrent jobs for the same target, and conflicting Check-All/Update-All work, are rejected safely
- normal and security update counts are calculated as separate fields; unknown values remain `Unknown` instead of becoming false zeroes
- DEBUG logging is configurable: normal output hides internal Proxmox/remote diagnostics while DEBUG mode keeps technical details available
- generic filter output consistently uses Target IDs, with clearer remote failures and one central filter summary per job
- configurable Web UI port with local CLI administration, conflict detection, atomic writes, and update/self-update preservation
- Systems inventory, node-card layout, configuration matrices, job output, zero-update summaries, and mobile presentation
- configuration migration and preservation of comments, unknown keys, user values, External legacy entries, and custom ports

Fixed:
- final non-zero status aggregation after continuing past target failures
- bounded remote cluster checks, SSH/SCP, QGA readiness, package-manager paths, and lifecycle restoration
- remote VM/LXC post-update status is imported centrally so successful refreshes do not remain stale or permanently pending
- Check never reboots a VM; reboot handling remains confined to the Update path and `REBOOT_IF_NEEDED`
- interrupted/transient job state handling and duplicate notification paths
- QEMU guest-exec exit/output handling and remote guest-ID resolution across the cluster
- stale/duplicate inventory projections, node ordering, target-preview markers, orphaned zero-update lines, repeated remote filter banners, and node-card/checkbox hit-area overlap

Security/Safety:
- recent manual External backup verification or explicit one-time owner approval is required before External updates
- Proxmox snapshot and backup are independent protections; an unsupported snapshot does not silently enable a backup fallback, and configured backup modes/storage are validated
- Check operations are read-only with respect to rebooting: a Check never reboots a VM, while `REBOOT_IF_NEEDED` is evaluated only during Update operations
- TLS 1.2 or newer is required for HTTPS Web UI connections; the HTTPS port does not accept plaintext HTTP
- authenticated, CSRF- and same-origin-protected Web UI writes with no arbitrary command/file endpoint
- External helper access remains restricted; no `NOPASSWD: ALL`, unrestricted sudo, or secret transfer

Known limitations:
- Upgrading from older installations can require a host restart because of the changed job/service infrastructure; the updater does not reboot the host automatically.
- Windows support remains prepared/experimental and deferred from the supported Beta baseline pending dedicated live validation
- automatic External backup integrations are not implemented; manual time-bound verification remains the safety mechanism

